    "preview_note": "Applied Materials reports fiscal Q3 2026 results against elevated expectations fueled by robust AI infrastructure momentum, gate-all-around (GAA) logic transitions, and expanding high-bandwidth memory (HBM) capacity build-outs. Management\u2019s Q3 revenue guidance of $8.95B \u00b1 $500M and non-GAAP EPS of $3.36 \u00b1 $0.20 reflects accelerated wafer fab equipment (WFE) spending among key leading-edge foundry/logic and DRAM customers. We model Q3 revenue at $9,050M and non-GAAP EPS at $3.40, tracking slightly above midpoint given high delivery rates in advanced packaging and materials engineering systems. Key setup factors: (1) foundry/logic spending momentum as TSMC and Intel ramp 2nm and GAA nodes, driving adoption of AMAT\u2019s Trillium ALD and Precision selective PECVD systems; (2) DRAM/HBM expansion supporting materials engineering intensity; and (3) operational gross margin expansion to 50.2% on favorable product mix. The earnings reaction will hinge on Q4 guidance and management\u2019s update on calendar 2026 WFE growth expectations, where management previously signaled >30% growth in equipment revenue.",
    "reasoning": "Our forecast for AMAT's Q3 FY2026 anchors on strong execution in advanced process nodes (2nm GAA logic, HBM3e/HBM4 DRAM) and expanding advanced packaging equipment demand. Revenue of $9,050M tracks slightly above guidance midpoint ($8,950M). Non-GAAP gross margin expands to 50.16% driven by favorable product mix in Semiconductor Systems. All income statement, cash flow, and balance sheet identities strictly reconcile. Roll-forwards for cash_and_restricted ($6,359M + $580M = $6,939M) and retained_earnings ($59,274M + $2,720M - $420M - $500M = $61,074M) hold precisely."
